{
  "id": 489397535,
  "iid": 25122,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "csn1: fix printing of M_UINT_ARRAY items",
  "description": "Before this change, only the element count was printed for `M_UINT_ARRAY` items, while the actual array contents were omitted.\n\nOne possible approach would be to modify the format string passed to `proto_tree_add_uint_bits_format_value()` and print the value there.\nHowever, this would unnecessarily enforce a specific formatting style. Instead, use plain `proto_tree_add_bits_ret_val()` for value rendering.\nThis has the advantage of honoring the formatting defined in the hf_register_info array.  The count/index information is then appended\nseparately using `proto_item_append_text()`. The `_ret_val()` variant is used to avoid fetching item values twice.\n\nBelow is a fragment of GSM RLC/MAC `PACKET_SERVING_CELL_DATA` message contents before:\n\n```\n...\n        ...0 1100 = CONTAINER_INDEX: 12\n        0000 0011 = CONTAINER:  (Count 0)\n        0010 1011 = CONTAINER:  (Count 1)\n        0010 1011 = CONTAINER:  (Count 2)\n        0010 1011 = CONTAINER:  (Count 3)\n...\n```\n\nand afteer this change:\n\n```\n...\n        ...0 1100 = CONTAINER_INDEX: 12\n        0000 0011 = CONTAINER: 0x03 (count 0)\n        0010 1011 = CONTAINER: 0x2b (count 1)\n        0010 1011 = CONTAINER: 0x2b (count 2)\n        0010 1011 = CONTAINER: 0x2b (count 3)\n...\n```\n\nAI-Assisted: yes (Claude) - commit messages only",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2026-05-27T13:02:46.184Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-05-28T12:03:11.470Z",
